  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe structural underestimation: The model consistently forecasts a flat, mean-reverting trajectory (approx. 77-80 EUR) while the market exhibits a distinct upward regime shift (spiking to 88-91 EUR). Apply a regime-switching bias adjustment of +10 to +15 EUR when sentiment history shows sustained positive values (>= 0.67) following a volatility spike.",
    "Eliminate excessive lag in trend capture: The model fails to react to the breakout above 80 EUR, continuing to predict values near the historical mean. When the 3-day rolling average of true prices exceeds the forecast by >3 EUR, immediately override the model with a momentum-based projection rather than a mean-reverting one.",
    "Adjust for volatility clustering and overshoot: The model assumes low volatility and smooth convergence. In periods of high sentiment (1.00) and price spikes, increase the forecasted volatility envelope and allow for higher peaks (up to 92 EUR) rather than capping predictions near 80 EUR.",
    "Re-evaluate sentiment weighting: The model appears to ignore or under-weight positive sentiment signals (1.00) in favor of historical price averages. Increase the sensitivity of the forecast to recent positive sentiment spikes to capture the 'breakout' behavior observed in the true outcomes."
  ]
}
